1	# Supabase MCP Server
2	
3	![Supabase MCP Server](screen.png)
4	
5	A powerful Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Supabase, **built with [mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use)**. This server provides interactive tools and beautiful React widgets for exploring and querying your Supabase database.
6	
7	## 🚀 Built with mcp-use
8	
9	This MCP server is powered by **[mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use)**, a modern framework for building MCP servers with:
10	
11	- **Type-safe server creation** - Build MCP servers with full TypeScript support
12	- **React widget support** - Create interactive UI components using the OpenAI Apps SDK
13	- **Simplified client connections** - Easily connect to other MCP servers without LangChain
14	- **Built-in development tools** - Hot reload, build, and deploy commands
15	- **Zero boilerplate** - Focus on your tools, not infrastructure
16	
17	## Features
18	
19	- 🔍 **Database Schema Explorer** - Browse all tables in your Supabase database with an interactive UI
20	- 📊 **Table Viewer** - Display and explore table data with a beautiful data table widget
21	- 🔎 **SQL Query Executor** - Run read-only SQL queries and view results in an interactive widget
22	- 🎨 **React Widgets** - Rich, interactive UI components built with React and Tailwind CSS
23	- 🔐 **Secure Authentication** - Uses Supabase Personal Access Tokens for secure access
24	
25	## Prerequisites
26	
27	- Node.js 18+ and yarn
28	- A Supabase project
29	- A Supabase Personal Access Token ([generate one here](https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens))
30	
31	## Installation
32	
33	```bash
34	# Install dependencies
35	yarn install
36	```
37	
38	## Configuration
39	
40	Set the following required environment variables:
41	
42	```bash
43	# Required: Your Supabase Personal Access Token
44	export ACCESS_TOKEN="your-access-token"
45	
46	# Required: Content Security Policy URLs for widget loading => required by ChatGPT
47	export CSP_URLS="https://supabase.com,https://mcp.supabase.com,https://*.mcp-use.com,https://*.supabase.co"
48	```
49	
50	## Development
51	
52	[mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use) provides convenient development commands:
53	
54	```bash
55	# Start development server with hot reload
56	yarn dev
57	
58	# Build for production
59	yarn build
60	
61	# Start production server
62	yarn start
63	
64	# Deploy the server
65	yarn deploy
66	```
67	
68	## Available Tools
69	
70	### `list-tables`
71	
72	List all tables in your Supabase database. Opens an interactive schema explorer widget.
73	
74	**Parameters:**
75	
76	- `schemas` (optional): Array of schema names to include (default: `["public"]`)
77	
78	**Widget:** `schema-explorer` - Interactive table browser with schema information
79	
80	### `show-table`
81	
82	Display data from a specific table. Opens a data table viewer widget.
83	
84	**Parameters:**
85	
86	- `tableName` (required): Name of the table to display
87	- `schema` (optional): Schema name (default: `"public"`)
88	- `limit` (optional): Maximum number of rows to fetch (default: `100`)
89	
90	**Widget:** `table-viewer` - Interactive data table with sorting and filtering
91	
92	### `execute-sql`
93	
94	Execute read-only SQL queries on your Supabase database. Opens a query results widget.
95	
96	**Parameters:**
97	
98	- `query` (required): SQL query to execute
99	
100	**Widget:** `query-results` - Interactive query results viewer with syntax highlighting
101	
102	## Available Resources
103	
104	### `supabase://project-url`
105	
106	Get the API URL for your Supabase project.
107	
108	## UI Widgets
109	
110	This server includes three custom React widgets built with [mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use):
111	
112	1. **Schema Explorer** (`schema-explorer`) - Browse database tables and schemas
113	2. **Table Viewer** (`table-viewer`) - View and explore table data
114	3. **Query Results** (`query-results`) - Display SQL query results
115	
116	All widgets are built with:
117	
118	- React 19
119	- Tailwind CSS
120	- Radix UI components
121	- Lucide React icons
122	
123	## Architecture
124	
125	This server demonstrates the power of [mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use):
126	
127	- **Server-side**: Uses [`mcp-use/server`](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use) to create tools, resources, and widgets
128	- **Client-side**: Uses [`mcp-use/client`](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use) to connect to Supabase's official MCP server
129	- **No LangChain**: Direct MCP client connections without external dependencies
130	- **Type-safe**: Full TypeScript support with Zod schemas
131	
132	## Project Structure
133	
134	```
135	.
136	├── index.ts                 # Main server file using [mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use)
137	├── resources/               # React widget components
138	│   ├── components/         # Reusable UI components
139	│   ├── schema-explorer/    # Schema explorer widget
140	│   ├── table-viewer/       # Table viewer widget
141	│   ├── supabase-status/    # Display Supabase status for a certain time window
142	│   └── query-results/      # Query results widget
143	└── package.json            # Dependencies including [mcp-use](https://github.com/mcp-use/mcp-use)
144	```
145	
